{"step_index":600,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-08-24T22:59:40Z","content":"The Reference Panel on both the front end and back end has been unified into a single, authoritative **Service Rubrics Digest**.\n\n---\n\n### What Changed & How Duplication Was Removed\n\n#### 1. Frontend Layout Unification ([index.html](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/index.html#L183-L220))\n* **Removed Redundant Tab Switcher**: Deleted the `.reference-tabs` bar (`btn-ref-tab-digest` vs `btn-ref-tab-service-digest`) and the duplicate `#doc-digest` container.\n* **Unified into Single Panel**: The Reference Panel now has one unified header (`📖 Service Rubrics Digest`) and one structured document container (`#service-digest-content`).\n* **Clean Dropdown Selector**: The `View Office` dropdown allows viewing **All Services (Full Typikon Digest)** or filtering directly to a specific office (*General Info*, *Vespers*, *Compline*, *Midnight Office*, *Matins*, *Hours*, *Divine Liturgy*).\n\n#### 2. Frontend Logic Streamlining ([main.js](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/main.js#L54-L65))\n* **Single Source of Truth**: Removed the separate `renderDigestHtml()` function. All rubrics rendering flows through the structured `renderServiceDigestContent()` function.\n* **Unified Copy Action**: The copy button (`#btn-copy-digest`) copies the complete Markdown digest when \"All Services\" is selected, or copies the exact isolated service text when filtered.\n* **Eliminated Dead State**: Removed obsolete `selectedRefTab` state and event listeners.\n\n#### 3. Backend Pipeline Integrity ([server.py](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/server.py#L306-L355))\n* The backend returns a single, canonical `digest` string from `RuthenianEngine.generate_typikon_digest()`.\n* There are no competing endpoints or parallel data streams for the digest; the frontend parses the canonical markdown sections directly.\n\n---\n\n### Verification\n* Server endpoint tests passed (`tests/test_server_endpoints.py`: **6 passed in 16.68s**).\n* Session compliance passed (`tests/test_session_compliance.py`: **1 passed in 0.36s**).\n\n---\n\n### Next Step: Canonical Typikon Source Audit\nNow that the UI pipeline is unified and clean, we can canonically audit the digest output against the **2010 Lviv Typikon / Dolnytsky Typikon Part II**. \n\nWhich benchmark date would you like to start auditing first? (e.g. An ordinary Sunday with simple saint, a Sunday colliding with a Polyeleos saint, or a Great Feast).\n\n---\n### Summary of Work\n* Merged the two separate Reference Panel tabs into a single unified **Service Rubrics Digest** in [index.html](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/index.html).\n* Refactored [main.js](file:///c:/Users/augus/OneDrive/Documents/Google%20Antigravity/Projects/Typikon%20Coded/cantor_dashboard/main.js) to route all rubric formatting through one consolidated rendering pipeline.\n* Verified that all backend and server tests pass without errors."}
